# Finite independent group editor review

This review authenticates the frozen885 candidate and the two root21 source-bound HTTP/browser records. The preserved original managed-library load count22 is historical author evidence. This reviewer does not run an original, shared host, browser or benchmark unless a confirmed concern needs that separate campaign.

Fresh case design follows the actual client/server source, before reading authored group-edit test bodies. A source hypothesis is a later group-list response after successful Create/Save: enabled name/notes changes made while that list response is held may be erased by the unconditional group-form replacement. Probe both the first active-list and second group-list waits, and retain genuine failures distinctly from fixture mistakes.

Other selected cases cover newly created UUID/MAC continuation after a newer draft, existing-group rename with selected-entry restrictions, newer entry draft preservation, group/bin/list invalidation, a failed persistence write and retry, disposal, and immutable server request capture while queued. A DOM model is not native browser acceptance. A reused canonical fixture may supply native metadata, but the case bodies, expectations and delayed boundaries are independently selected. Synthetic master passwords and IDs are disposable test data only. No application or production sources are edited.

One initial source-only read guessed group-edit.mjs; that module does not exist because group-edit primitives are exported by recycle.mjs. No program was executed by that failed read and no candidate/product failure is inferred.
